---
layout: base.jinja
title: Examples
description: Small, complete sites built with SiteSquatch, each distilled from a real one or a study and written against a feature, running live with their source a click away.
permalink: /examples/
---
{%- from "drawing.jinja" import drawing with context -%}
<section class="gallery">
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="stop-head">
			<div>
				<p class="kicker">Campsites</p>
				<h1>Examples</h1>
				<p class="lead">Small, complete sites, each distilled from a real one and written against a feature of ssqch. The test suite builds and link-checks every one, and each runs here, built under its own path. Poke around the live site, then take what you need from the source: copy its folder and run <code>ssqch serve</code> in it.</p>
			</div>
			{{ drawing("stickers/tent", 120, class="stop-art", eager=true) }}
		</div>
		<ul class="campsites">
			{%- for example in examples %}
			<li id="{{ example.name }}">
				<h2><code>{{ example.name }}</code></h2>
				<p class="engine">{{ example.engine }} · distilled from {{ example.from }}</p>
				<p>{{ example.shows }}</p>
				<ul class="features">
					{%- for feature in example.features %}
					<li><a href="{{ feature.docs }}">{{ feature.label }}</a></li>
					{%- endfor %}
				</ul>
				<p class="links"><a class="button" href="/examples/{{ example.name }}/">Visit the live site</a> <a class="button quiet" href="{{ site.repo }}/tree/main/examples/sites/{{ example.name }}">Source</a></p>
			</li>
			{%- endfor %}
		</ul>
	</div>
</section>
